From 0c7dc1f0fc0bbdb53d029c8927c6201a227481fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Boyd <danieljboyd@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:33:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] x11, cairo: popover shadows for menus, when a theme asks

GNOME's menus are popovers: rounded, with a soft shadow of their own,
fainter and shorter than a window's.  A theme that draws GNUstep's menus
that way can round their corners with the alpha channel for borderless
windows, but has nowhere to draw the shadow.

A borderless window marked with NSUtilityWindowMask, which a borderless
window has no other use for, is treated as a popover when the new
GSBackPopoverShadows default is YES: it gets a transparent margin like a
window's (14 points at the sides, 12 above, 16 below), on a window's
terms (the gui draws the decorations, the window manager knows
_GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS, a compositing manager runs), corners rounded by
GSBackPopoverCornerRadius, and no resize band: presses land only in its
visible part.  The shadow is libadwaita's popover box-shadow, "0 1px 5px
1px" black at 0.09 and "0 2px 14px 3px" black at 0.05, computed as a CSS
blur from the distance to the popover's rounded outline, so it follows
the corners as a browser's does.  Only libadwaita's published numbers are
taken; no code.  The shadow template cache keeps one template for
windows and one for popovers.  Nothing changes unless the default is set
and a window is marked.

Testing: both shadow tests from the previous change gain popover cases.
Tests/x11/shadowmargin.m checks that a marked window has no margin
without the default; with it, the popover's exact margin, X window size
and input shape (the visible part only, no band); and that the default
gives no margin to an unmarked borderless window and doesn't change a
titled window's.  Tests/x11/shadowdrawing.m makes a borderless,
NSUtilityWindowMask NSPanel and reads its pixels back: contents opaque,
corners rounded off, about 8% black beside it fading to nearly nothing
at its margin's edge, and stronger below than above (values seen: 21 and
1 across the margin, 26 below, 16 above, against 46, 51 and 22 for a
window).  Without this change the popover margin check fails and the
popover's drawing checks can't run (its X window has no margin); with
it, shadowmargin.m passes 23 of 23 and shadowdrawing.m 14 of 14.

AI assistance: this change, its tests and this description were written
with Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
